breadcrumbs are a runtime switch everywhere except here, and here shouts 46,591 times.

vkd3d has two independent breadcrumb switches and they are not the same thing:

  * `VKD3D_ENABLE_BREADCRUMBS`, a **compile-time** define, decides whether the
    code exists at all;
  * `VKD3D_CONFIG_FLAG_BREADCRUMBS`, a **runtime** flag from `VKD3D_CONFIG`,
    decides whether it does anything.

Thirty-six of the thirty-seven `#ifdef VKD3D_ENABLE_BREADCRUMBS` sites check the
runtime flag inside the ifdef -- the placed-resource registration eleven lines
below this one is the closest example, and `d3d12_resource_destroy` does the same
on the way out. This one does not. It sets
`initial_layout_transition_validate_only` on every placed RTV and DSV the moment
the build has breadcrumbs compiled in, whether or not anybody asked for a trace.

What that flag does is turn `vk_image_memory_barrier_for_initial_transition` into
a reporting function: it logs and returns false instead of filling in a barrier.
The `false` is correct and matches the release path -- see the comment right
above, which is upstream's reason for not transitioning placed render targets
itself: on hardware with DCC/HTILE the initialization would clobber other buffers
aliased into the same heap. The logging is not correct, because nothing turned it
on.

**Measured on Resident Evil Requiem, 2026-08-16: 46,591 lines in one session,
93% of the log**, all of them this one message, at ERR so no severity setting
quiets it. Two separate costs, and the second is the one that matters:

  * a formatted `ERR` with a `debug_dxgi_format` call per placed resource per
    submission, on the render thread;
  * **it hid a real graphics bug in plain sight.** With 93% of the log one
    repeated line, the session was unreadable, and the message that says
    *"this resource was never initialized"* -- next to screenshots of a flat
    white quad where geometry should be -- read as noise rather than as the
    answer.

So gate it on the runtime flag like every other site. A build with breadcrumbs
compiled in then behaves exactly like a release build until `VKD3D_CONFIG`
contains `breadcrumbs`, which is what makes the whole instrument usable from a
settings screen instead of from a second build nobody has.

**That is the point of this patch, and it is worth stating plainly.**
`build/vkd3d.sh` logs "diagnostic build, not for shipping" when `VKD3D_BREADCRUMBS=1`,
and it was right to: the build was unusable as a default because of this line.
With it fixed the remaining cost of shipping breadcrumbs is `-Denable_trace=true`,
which is binary size rather than output -- every TRACE is still gated behind
`VKD3D_DEBUG`, which Vessel pins at `fixme`. In exchange, the one instrument in
the stack that can explain a `VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST` stops requiring a rebuild at
the moment somebody needs it, which is always the worst moment to need one.

Note this changes no rendering. Both branches leave the resource untransitioned
-- `initial_layout_transition = 0` makes the callers skip it, `validate_only`
makes the barrier builder decline it -- so the only difference is whether a line
is printed. `force_initial_transition` remains the switch that changes behaviour,
and it is checked before either.

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/resource.c b/libs/vkd3d/resource.c
--- a/libs/vkd3d/resource.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/resource.c
@@ -4614,11 +4614,25 @@
     if (desc->Flags & (D3D12_RESOURCE_FLAG_ALLOW_RENDER_TARGET | D3D12_RESOURCE_FLAG_ALLOW_DEPTH_STENCIL))
     {
         if (!(vkd3d_config_flags & VKD3D_CONFIG_FLAG_FORCE_INITIAL_TRANSITION))
         {
 #ifdef VKD3D_ENABLE_BREADCRUMBS
-            object->initial_layout_transition_validate_only = true;
+            /* Vessel: the runtime flag, not merely the compile-time one.
+             *
+             * Every other breadcrumb site in this file checks it -- the placed
+             * resource registration eleven lines down, and the unregister in
+             * d3d12_resource_destroy. Without it a build with breadcrumbs
+             * compiled in reports every placed RTV and DSV on every submission
+             * whether or not a trace was asked for: 46,591 lines and 93% of one
+             * Requiem session, at ERR, where they buried the graphics bug they
+             * were describing. Behaviour is identical either way -- both
+             * branches leave the resource untransitioned -- so this only decides
+             * whether the line is printed. */
+            if (vkd3d_config_flags & VKD3D_CONFIG_FLAG_BREADCRUMBS)
+                object->initial_layout_transition_validate_only = true;
+            else
+                object->initial_layout_transition = 0;
 #else
             object->initial_layout_transition = 0;
 #endif
         }
     }
